  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local financing solutions to support Jordan#s agri-food system transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint Programme (JP) will catalyze the transformation of Jordan#s fruits and vegetables (F&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;V) sector into an inclusive, cl imate-resilient, and market-driven agrifood system. It will support the formation of rural alliances involving over 3,150 smallholder farmers, organized through 106 agricultural organizations and MSMEs, with strong emphasis on the inclusion of women, youth, and re fugees, alongside buyers, municipalities, and financial service providers. The JP will co-finance the adoption of climate-smart technologies and practices and establish two post-harvest centers. At least 70% of participating farmer groups and enterprises are expected to increase their annual incomes by approximately US$10,000 to US$12,000. The post-harvest centers in Deir Alla and Mafraq, each with a capacity of 30,000 metric tons per year, will reduce post-harvest losses by up to 30% and cut water use per unit of yield by 20%, while serving as critical hubs for rural market integration. Combined with the development of inclusive farmers# markets and piloting of public procurement schemes, as well as off-take agreements with retailers, the JP will strengthen linkages between smallholders and both high-value and institutional markets, improving incomes, food access, and system resilience at the subnational level.  The JP#</narrative>
  </description>
